worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_05.js"
  ceiling 1415
  rationale "Part of the mechanically split browser mirror of the Rust solver: issue #658 divided one oversized worker file by line count, so this shard has no subject of its own. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into js/wasm-worker. Ceiling moved 1466 to 1471 for issue #1173 R3 (2026-10-07): the year-count reader no longer stops at the "year" of "compounded yearly", and the CSV-to-JSON request gets its reader, so probes p069 and p119 reach their handlers in both runtimes. Ceiling moved to 1474 for issue #1175 R3 (follow-up round, 2026-10-08): the brainstorm, roleplay, previous-message recall and translation arms record their named refusal events when they answer without their input, and the translation answer now carries its evidence. Lowered to 1465 for issue #918 (2026-10-08): tryKupiSlona answers through the kupi_slona rule of data/seed/handler-rules.lino instead of an inline Russian text. Lowered to 1454 the same day: the brainstorm count policy is the seed default_count and count_cardinal, and the roleplay fallbacks are the seed alone. Ceiling moved to 1460 the same day: tryFactLookup renders a release-timeline record against today instead of reading a summary the record does not carry. Lowered to 1415 the same day: tryCompoundInterest reads its periods, labels, default rates and final-amount marker from the policy compound_interest block of data/seed/handler-rules.lino and its wording from seeded responses, as the native handler does."
